      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-05-28T21:26:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Usually the caller is passed the out_msg pointer in which to store its response, and calls shi_reply_response() passing that same pointer back as msg_ptr.\n\nHowever, the caller may also pass a different pointer back (for example, if it\u0027s passing back static data).  In that case, we need to copy the msg_ptr into our own output buffer.\n\nThis is more of an issue on the STM32 chips, which can do DMA directly from msg_ptr instead of needing a copy.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 185,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 188,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "138733a324803332c34d79f3f4ca15fd6e846106",
